    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel like burnout though. burnout implies you can rest and come back. this feels more like... permanent decay. like the well ran dry and there's just dust at the bottom. i look at my old work and i don't even recognize that person. i feel like i'm just haunting my own life. why should i keep trying to scrape at the bottom of a dry well when there's nothing left to find?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of permanent decay is incredibly heavy, and it's completely understandable why you feel hopeless about continuing. When the well seems entirely dry, the thought of forcing yourself to \"scrape\" feels pointless and exhausting. Instead of looking for a source to refill, maybe it's time to simply honor the stillness you are in right now. It doesn't have to be about creating or \"fixing\" anything; sometimes the most important thing is just allowing yourself to exist without the pressure of performance.",
      "source": "target",
